WEBVTT

00:00:02.270 --> 00:00:06.170
Would you like to see the photos 
Mochizuki-san took at the Christmas party?

00:00:02.940 --> 00:00:08.940
<b>Winter Break
Open Today Only</b>

00:00:06.170 --> 00:00:07.850
Yes, I would.

00:00:07.850 --> 00:00:08.940
Me, too.

00:00:09.610 --> 00:00:10.590
Here you go.

00:00:13.760 --> 00:00:16.320
It was a lot of fun.

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:17.840
Yeah, it was.

00:00:17.840 --> 00:00:20.330
I'm glad Chloe-san didn't have to go home.

00:00:21.010 --> 00:00:23.500
Everyone seemed to be having a great time.

00:00:25.860 --> 00:00:30.170
Neuron Cream Soft's performance 
was really exciting, too.

00:00:32.680 --> 00:00:35.530
Though there was that scare with the cake.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:42.350
Miyoshi-san and Chloe-san's 
costumes were really cute.

00:00:43.740 --> 00:00:45.100
The gift exchange was fun, too.

00:00:55.510 --> 00:00:58.120
I want to get together with everyone again.

00:00:58.480 --> 00:00:59.870
Yeah.

00:00:59.870 --> 00:01:00.830
Definitely.

00:01:00.830 --> 00:01:02.070
Hi, there.

00:01:02.070 --> 00:01:06.580
Fumio-san, lend me a book on New Year's, please.

00:01:06.580 --> 00:01:08.790
A book on New Year's?

00:01:08.790 --> 00:01:11.560
Christmas is gone from the town.

00:01:11.560 --> 00:01:13.460
Everything is New Year's now.

00:01:13.760 --> 00:01:14.840
Huh?

00:01:15.230 --> 00:01:21.760
In Europe, many people still have 
their Christmas tree up in January.

00:01:21.760 --> 00:01:26.390
But here, as soon as Christmas 
is over, everything's gone.

00:01:26.840 --> 00:01:29.750
Wow, so that's what they do in Europe?

00:01:29.750 --> 00:01:31.810
Wait just a moment.

00:01:34.010 --> 00:01:37.320
The New Year's mood is already everywhere.

00:01:37.320 --> 00:01:41.100
Including around town, and in TV commercials.

00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:45.470
If you're interested in learning more 
about New Year's, how about this?

00:01:49.380 --> 00:01:51.380
There's a lot of kanji.

00:01:51.380 --> 00:01:53.680
It looks a bit hard.

00:01:53.680 --> 00:01:56.300
Maybe this one is too difficult for you two.

00:01:57.900 --> 00:01:59.930
Chloe-san, Yulia-san.

00:02:00.280 --> 00:02:03.980
Would you like to come to my
house for New Year's Eve?

00:02:03.980 --> 00:02:05.930
Your house?

00:02:06.330 --> 00:02:09.560
Yes. We don't do anything special,

00:02:09.560 --> 00:02:13.320
but you'd get to see a typical 
Japanese New Year's that way.

00:02:14.160 --> 00:02:15.590
That's a good idea!

00:02:15.590 --> 00:02:17.630
Can I come, too?

00:02:17.630 --> 00:02:19.510
Yes, of course!

00:02:19.510 --> 00:02:22.440
Would you like to come, too, Murakami-senpai?

00:02:22.440 --> 00:02:24.510
If it's not too much trouble.

00:02:24.510 --> 00:02:25.650
Of course not!

00:02:25.650 --> 00:02:27.080
Please, come over.

00:02:28.900 --> 00:02:30.960
We can't wait!

00:04:01.030 --> 00:04:04.700
<b>Girlfriend xxx</b>

00:04:01.670 --> 00:04:02.840
Kadomatsu!

00:04:03.600 --> 00:04:04.840
Shimenawa!

00:04:07.430 --> 00:04:09.850
Japanese culture is so wonderful!

00:04:14.940 --> 00:04:18.470
It's my first time seeing 
something so beautiful!

00:04:18.470 --> 00:04:19.440
Très bien!

00:04:20.050 --> 00:04:22.790
Everyone puts these up for New Year's, though.

00:04:22.790 --> 00:04:25.320
Mochizuki-senpai couldn't come?

00:04:26.010 --> 00:04:30.760
I bet she would have loved to see you 
two get so excited about kadomatsu.

00:04:30.760 --> 00:04:32.960
I tried asking her, but...

00:04:33.730 --> 00:04:36.470
What?! I want to go!

00:04:36.470 --> 00:04:40.170
But I have something to do on New Year's Eve...

00:04:40.730 --> 00:04:42.920
It seemed like she was too busy.

00:04:43.600 --> 00:04:45.150
That's too bad.

00:04:45.820 --> 00:04:47.840
Let's go inside.

00:04:47.840 --> 00:04:48.800
Sure.

00:04:51.370 --> 00:04:53.180
Osechi!

00:04:54.980 --> 00:04:56.830
This is fantastic.

00:04:56.830 --> 00:04:58.810
It all looks so delicious.

00:05:00.190 --> 00:05:02.360
You flatter me, but thank you.

00:05:02.360 --> 00:05:05.240
So, you're curious about New Year's in Japan?

00:05:05.240 --> 00:05:06.030
Yes.

00:05:06.800 --> 00:05:08.820
Do you know what this is?

00:05:09.170 --> 00:05:12.160
A nice ornament?

00:05:12.160 --> 00:05:16.790
No, it's a, um... A racket.

00:05:18.020 --> 00:05:21.660
If you lose, you get an 
"x" drawn on your face.

00:05:21.660 --> 00:05:22.720
An "x"?

00:05:22.720 --> 00:05:26.090
You get an "x" drawn on your 
face with charcoal as a penalty.

00:05:28.280 --> 00:05:31.570
Murakami-senpai, I think Chloe-senpai is imagining

00:05:31.570 --> 00:05:35.370
some sort of terrible misunderstanding 
about Japanese culture again.

00:05:35.370 --> 00:05:37.600
Like with the mochi.

00:05:38.040 --> 00:05:40.360
I won't make that mistake again.

00:05:41.920 --> 00:05:45.620
There are also kites, and the iroha karuta game.

00:05:45.620 --> 00:05:47.070
And otedama.

00:05:48.360 --> 00:05:50.470
You're just like Emi-san.

00:05:51.070 --> 00:05:52.530
Emi-san?

00:05:52.530 --> 00:05:54.690
You mean Sagara-san in Kokomi's class?

00:05:54.690 --> 00:05:55.930
That's right.

00:05:55.930 --> 00:05:58.420
She's really good at juggling.

00:05:58.420 --> 00:05:59.460
I see.

00:05:59.460 --> 00:06:08.970
<b>Iroha Karuta</b>

00:06:00.480 --> 00:06:04.070
Since we have so many people, 
the iroha karuta game might be best.

00:06:04.070 --> 00:06:06.310
You'd also get to learn Japanese sayings.

00:06:06.310 --> 00:06:08.020
Let's all play.

00:06:08.020 --> 00:06:08.970
Sure!

00:06:11.910 --> 00:06:14.450
Harumiya-san, Kumada-san, your turn.

00:06:14.450 --> 00:06:15.880
All right!

00:06:14.450 --> 00:06:15.880
Sure.

00:06:18.790 --> 00:06:19.760
Hit it!

00:06:22.980 --> 00:06:23.440
There we go.

00:06:24.470 --> 00:06:26.270
This really helps us out.

00:06:26.270 --> 00:06:29.140
At our age, it's tough to do this.

00:06:29.140 --> 00:06:30.910
It's hard on the lower back, isn't it?

00:06:40.630 --> 00:06:41.420
There!

00:06:43.290 --> 00:06:44.710
All right, that's good!

00:06:45.060 --> 00:06:47.210
Huh? It's done already?

00:06:49.370 --> 00:06:51.770
Never underestimate the stamina...

00:06:51.770 --> 00:06:53.800
...of athletes.

00:06:59.540 --> 00:07:01.400
Want some mochi?

00:07:01.400 --> 00:07:03.270
I will have some.

00:07:03.270 --> 00:07:06.320
Eating something as sticky as mochi is...

00:07:10.630 --> 00:07:12.380
Monochrome-chan!

00:07:12.380 --> 00:07:13.530
Did she choke?

00:07:13.940 --> 00:07:15.710
We need to clear her throat.

00:07:15.710 --> 00:07:18.790
Nah, no need to worry.

00:07:19.290 --> 00:07:22.880
Monochrome-chan doesn't breathe, anyway.

00:07:23.480 --> 00:07:26.390
So she can't choke.

00:07:36.690 --> 00:07:38.520
...a first for me.

00:07:42.990 --> 00:07:44.270
So cute!

00:07:44.270 --> 00:07:45.940
So very cute!

00:07:45.940 --> 00:07:47.540
You look like a doll.

00:07:47.540 --> 00:07:49.490
Don't look so closely!

00:07:49.490 --> 00:07:51.890
Why try to hide them?

00:07:51.890 --> 00:07:55.160
Yeah, you're really cute.

00:07:55.160 --> 00:07:57.250
I'm jealous.

00:07:57.250 --> 00:08:00.720
I've never worn a kimono.

00:08:00.720 --> 00:08:02.160
Neither have I.

00:08:02.420 --> 00:08:05.640
Oh, but you two would look great in a kimono.

00:08:06.440 --> 00:08:08.250
I'd love to help you put one on.

00:08:09.800 --> 00:08:10.990
Non, non.

00:08:10.990 --> 00:08:12.010
I couldn't.

00:08:12.010 --> 00:08:13.990
It'd be too embarrassing.

00:08:13.990 --> 00:08:15.220
Oh, really?

00:08:15.220 --> 00:08:16.520
It would.

00:08:16.520 --> 00:08:17.260
Yes...

00:08:17.700 --> 00:08:19.690
How very modest.

00:08:19.690 --> 00:08:21.680
Just like a classical Japanese woman.

00:08:21.680 --> 00:08:25.610
Mom, didn't we have a kimono?

00:08:25.610 --> 00:08:28.690
We gave yours to our relatives.

00:08:28.690 --> 00:08:30.810
It was one from when you were small, anyway.

00:08:30.810 --> 00:08:32.860
It wouldn't fit.

00:08:32.860 --> 00:08:33.940
Oh, I know.

00:08:33.940 --> 00:08:37.280
Shiranui-san probably has lots of them.

00:08:37.830 --> 00:08:41.990
She said she spends her time at home in kimonos.

00:08:41.990 --> 00:08:44.040
Why don't we ask her?

00:08:44.980 --> 00:08:46.140
I see.

00:08:46.140 --> 00:08:47.670
I wouldn't mind.

00:08:48.000 --> 00:08:49.290
She said okay.

00:08:49.290 --> 00:08:50.340
Yay!

00:08:50.340 --> 00:08:51.220
That's wonderful.

00:08:51.220 --> 00:08:52.380
I'm so glad.

00:08:52.380 --> 00:08:54.200
Are you sure it's okay?

00:08:54.200 --> 00:08:55.030
Sure.

00:08:55.030 --> 00:08:58.270
I'll get out something that'll suit you two.

00:08:59.050 --> 00:09:01.180
Isuzu-chan, what's going on?

00:09:01.680 --> 00:09:04.180
Turns out there's something I need to do.

00:09:04.760 --> 00:09:06.670
Help me out, Haruko.

00:09:06.670 --> 00:09:08.190
Sure.

00:09:09.370 --> 00:09:10.930
Okay, be careful.

00:09:10.930 --> 00:09:13.410
Don't stay out too late.

00:09:13.410 --> 00:09:14.630
Okay!

00:09:15.390 --> 00:09:19.950
What should we do after we go to 
Isuzu-san's house and put on kimonos?

00:09:19.950 --> 00:09:26.160
Our goal today is to teach you and 
Yulia-san about the Japanese New Year,

00:09:26.160 --> 00:09:31.920
so we should go to a temple, ring the 
New Year's bell, and visit a shrine to pray.

00:09:31.920 --> 00:09:35.330
Oui! That sounds like a lot of fun!

00:09:35.330 --> 00:09:39.460
We need to make sure you 
completely understand what to do.

00:09:39.460 --> 00:09:42.740
Or you might get something mixed up again.

00:09:43.770 --> 00:09:45.920
I'll be fine.

00:09:45.920 --> 00:09:48.210
I'll get rid of my worldly desires.

00:09:49.800 --> 00:09:52.280
"Worldly desires"? What's that?

00:09:52.280 --> 00:09:57.340
Worldly desires are the worries and 
desires that we have as humans.

00:09:57.340 --> 00:10:01.810
We ring the New Year's bell in order 
to rid ourselves of those desires.

00:10:01.810 --> 00:10:04.730
You know everything, don't you, Fumio-san?

00:10:04.730 --> 00:10:07.500
You're a walking encyclopedia.

00:10:09.950 --> 00:10:11.210
Welcome.

00:10:11.670 --> 00:10:13.080
Hi, there.

00:10:13.080 --> 00:10:14.780
You've been shopping?

00:10:14.780 --> 00:10:15.950
Yeah.

00:10:15.950 --> 00:10:17.380
We've been through a lot.

00:10:18.120 --> 00:10:22.290
Remi said we should do New Year's stuff 
for once, so we went to help,

00:10:22.290 --> 00:10:24.830
and she nearly messed up everything.

00:10:26.220 --> 00:10:27.810
Sorry about that.

00:10:28.240 --> 00:10:31.060
I wonder why everything turned out so bad.

00:10:31.060 --> 00:10:33.420
I was following the directions.

00:10:33.420 --> 00:10:34.660
You were?

00:10:34.660 --> 00:10:39.140
You weren't following the directions. 
You kept making changes.

00:10:39.140 --> 00:10:42.380
Like using marmalade instead of sugar.

00:10:42.380 --> 00:10:46.330
I thought marmalade would be a good 
substitute for the sugar and citrus.

00:10:46.330 --> 00:10:47.830
I wasn't wrong, was I?

00:10:47.830 --> 00:10:49.240
Well...

00:10:49.240 --> 00:10:50.250
Here you go.

00:10:50.660 --> 00:10:56.600
Tamai-san, I think using marmalade 
for sugar is a great idea.

00:10:56.600 --> 00:10:58.720
I'll try it next time I have a chance.

00:10:59.120 --> 00:11:00.030
Huh?

00:11:02.150 --> 00:11:06.390
Nonoka-san, what happened to the owner?

00:11:06.390 --> 00:11:10.140
He's out at a neighborhood 
gathering to make mochi.

00:11:10.420 --> 00:11:11.660
Huh?

00:11:11.660 --> 00:11:13.520
So, who's doing the cooking, then?

00:11:13.520 --> 00:11:15.570
No need to worry.

00:11:15.570 --> 00:11:18.240
I'll pour my heart and soul into your food!

00:11:20.990 --> 00:11:22.490
Nonoka, I'm back.

00:11:23.000 --> 00:11:24.160
Grandpa.

00:11:24.160 --> 00:11:25.540
Oh, hello.

00:11:25.540 --> 00:11:26.490
What's that?

00:11:26.850 --> 00:11:31.740
Are you guys after the neighborhood 
specialty, our roasted soybean mochi?

00:11:31.740 --> 00:11:33.740
We just finished making it, so it's tasty.

00:11:35.360 --> 00:11:36.710
We'll take it!

00:11:39.350 --> 00:11:41.890
Yuzu-chan, eating New Year's 
soba here at your house

00:11:41.890 --> 00:11:43.910
really makes it feel like the year's end.

00:11:43.910 --> 00:11:44.800
Really?

00:11:44.800 --> 00:11:46.880
You two have known each other forever.

00:11:46.880 --> 00:11:48.720
Do you always spend New Year's together?

00:11:48.720 --> 00:11:49.600
Yeah.

00:11:49.600 --> 00:11:52.180
Is it okay to leave your parents alone?

00:11:52.180 --> 00:11:55.660
It's cold, so they said they'd just
get some food delivered.

00:11:57.120 --> 00:11:58.980
Isn't that Yukawa-san?

00:11:59.350 --> 00:12:00.990
From Haruka's class.

00:12:01.780 --> 00:12:13.040
<b>Seiou Academy Second-year
Kise Yukawa-san</b>

00:12:01.780 --> 00:12:13.040
<b>A high school girl makes
a huge discovery!!</b>

00:12:02.160 --> 00:12:04.040
I left the instruments as they were,

00:12:04.040 --> 00:12:06.280
and went on to the next experiment.

00:12:06.280 --> 00:12:10.530
That was all that led to my surprising discovery.

00:12:10.530 --> 00:12:13.040
It's nothing worth congratulating.

00:12:13.380 --> 00:12:15.300
I've never seen her without her glasses!

00:12:15.300 --> 00:12:16.170
Me, neither!

00:12:16.170 --> 00:12:18.250
She's cute.

00:12:18.690 --> 00:12:19.960
She really is.

00:12:20.390 --> 00:12:24.890
Actually, why are you guys 
eating cold morisoba?

00:12:24.890 --> 00:12:26.530
Isn't warm kakesoba the norm?

00:12:26.530 --> 00:12:28.280
It is cold out.

00:12:28.280 --> 00:12:30.310
Kakesoba would warm you up better.

00:12:30.780 --> 00:12:34.310
People in the Edo period used to eat morisoba.

00:12:34.840 --> 00:12:36.580
What? Really?

00:12:36.580 --> 00:12:38.000
I didn't know that.

00:12:38.000 --> 00:12:42.280
Also, kakesoba makes you 
have to go to the bathroom.

00:12:42.280 --> 00:12:45.080
I don't want that during the New Year's concert.

00:12:45.080 --> 00:12:47.280
That doesn't happen to me.

00:12:47.280 --> 00:12:48.780
You traitor!

00:12:49.120 --> 00:12:51.690
That's being a bit dramatic.

00:12:51.690 --> 00:12:56.470
Well, whatever kind of soba you have, 
it'll get soggy if you don't eat it now.

00:12:58.900 --> 00:13:01.420
Thank you for the meal.

00:13:01.420 --> 00:13:05.260
A lot happened this year, but...

00:13:05.260 --> 00:13:06.510
Next year...

00:13:06.510 --> 00:13:07.640
Let's have...

00:13:08.160 --> 00:13:10.060
...another great year!

00:13:15.040 --> 00:13:18.860
Senpai, want to stop for some soba?

00:13:18.860 --> 00:13:20.980
I'd like to, but I don't have the money.

00:13:21.310 --> 00:13:24.380
Huh? You weren't able to sell enough?

00:13:24.380 --> 00:13:30.180
No, I saw so much stuff that was nice this year.

00:13:30.180 --> 00:13:32.360
I ended up buying it all.

00:13:32.360 --> 00:13:37.870
That's... nice, I think... 
Or maybe I should offer condolences...

00:13:37.870 --> 00:13:38.850
Yeah...

00:13:42.570 --> 00:13:46.760
Compared to a fulfilled heart, 
an empty stomach is nothing!

00:13:48.640 --> 00:13:52.200
I'd like to treat you,

00:13:52.200 --> 00:13:55.810
but I put a lot into my cosplay this year.

00:13:59.100 --> 00:14:00.040
Wait a second.

00:14:00.040 --> 00:14:01.690
Something smells good.

00:14:05.910 --> 00:14:08.280
Oh? Himejima-chan and...

00:14:08.550 --> 00:14:10.290
Shinonome-san, too!

00:14:10.290 --> 00:14:11.280
Yo.

00:14:11.740 --> 00:14:12.940
Yeah.

00:14:12.940 --> 00:14:14.660
So, how was this year?

00:14:15.420 --> 00:14:19.680
We sold a lot, and we bought a lot.

00:14:20.140 --> 00:14:22.900
You two, have some sweet red bean soup.

00:14:22.900 --> 00:14:23.670
Sure!

00:14:25.830 --> 00:14:27.740
Let's eat.

00:14:29.400 --> 00:14:30.980
This is great!

00:14:30.980 --> 00:14:32.880
It warms me up.

00:14:32.880 --> 00:14:36.380
Oh, Shinonome-san and Himejima-san,

00:14:36.380 --> 00:14:38.580
you're not going to participate in ComiCon?

00:14:38.580 --> 00:14:41.320
Isn't it full of stuff you like?

00:14:41.320 --> 00:14:43.970
Nah, I don't have the stamina.

00:14:43.970 --> 00:14:46.350
I don't like being around that many people.

00:14:46.350 --> 00:14:51.140
I went to get some food from Shinonome's 
house today because I felt lazy,

00:14:51.140 --> 00:14:54.860
and she didn't have anything, 
even though it's New Year's Eve.

00:14:54.860 --> 00:14:56.610
You really don't have it together.

00:14:56.610 --> 00:15:00.460
It's pretty weird to come to someone else's 
house to get food on New Year's Eve, too.

00:15:00.460 --> 00:15:02.580
Birds of a feather.

00:15:02.920 --> 00:15:06.340
I don't think that's something you 
get to say about each other.

00:15:06.720 --> 00:15:09.880
I'd rather not be lumped in with her at all.

00:15:11.140 --> 00:15:13.350
Girl Friend BETA.

00:15:15.620 --> 00:15:18.540
What a very Japanese-style house.

00:15:18.540 --> 00:15:19.850
How wonderful.

00:15:20.780 --> 00:15:22.670
Welcome.

00:15:22.670 --> 00:15:24.810
We're ready.

00:15:25.400 --> 00:15:26.640
Come on in.

00:15:26.640 --> 00:15:29.280
Yumesaki-san, why are you here?

00:15:29.600 --> 00:15:32.140
We've been friends since we were young.

00:15:32.140 --> 00:15:35.370
We always spend New Year's together.

00:15:46.040 --> 00:15:50.030
Is this some sort of art exhibit?

00:15:50.030 --> 00:15:54.300
No, I just put together some kimonos 
I thought would look good on you guys.

00:15:54.670 --> 00:15:57.560
I feel like my life is flashing before my eyes.

00:15:58.680 --> 00:16:04.140
Chloe-san, I think you mean this is 
the happiest moment in your life.

00:16:04.140 --> 00:16:08.690
Oh, sorry. This is the 
happiest moment in my life!

00:16:08.690 --> 00:16:10.400
I feel great.

00:16:10.710 --> 00:16:12.870
That's good to hear.

00:16:14.530 --> 00:16:17.180
Chloe-san, how about this one?

00:16:17.180 --> 00:16:18.740
I think it'd look great on you.

00:16:19.230 --> 00:16:21.870
They're all lovely. It's hard to choose.

00:16:21.870 --> 00:16:25.330
It's hard to match patterns with everyday clothes.

00:16:25.330 --> 00:16:28.750
I wonder why they look so pretty 
when they're on a kimono.

00:16:28.750 --> 00:16:30.420
That's so true.

00:16:31.200 --> 00:16:32.970
I like this one.

00:16:33.260 --> 00:16:34.200
I see.

00:16:34.200 --> 00:16:36.120
You've got good sense.

00:16:36.120 --> 00:16:38.440
That's the one I'd recommend the most.

00:16:38.440 --> 00:16:40.720
Yeah, that one's really nice.

00:16:41.120 --> 00:16:44.350
I feel like a sazare-ishi (a pebble).

00:16:44.350 --> 00:16:45.760
Sazare-ishi?

00:16:45.760 --> 00:16:47.870
You mean the national anthem?

00:16:47.870 --> 00:16:50.590
You mean it feels like Japan?

00:16:50.590 --> 00:16:51.740
No!

00:16:52.200 --> 00:16:58.880
There's a story about sisters who get 
to wear beautiful things together.

00:16:58.880 --> 00:17:01.750
You mean the book Sasameyuki?

00:17:01.750 --> 00:17:03.450
Th-That was it!

00:17:03.450 --> 00:17:06.710
I'm making a lot of mistakes today.

00:17:06.710 --> 00:17:08.760
I guess I'm too excited.

00:17:11.400 --> 00:17:14.580
Okay, let's get those two dressed up.

00:17:17.330 --> 00:17:18.460
Hello?

00:17:18.460 --> 00:17:19.390
Mochizuki-san?

00:17:19.870 --> 00:17:22.440
I'm almost done here,

00:17:22.440 --> 00:17:24.890
so I'd like to meet up with you if I can.

00:17:25.340 --> 00:17:26.820
Bye.

00:17:27.640 --> 00:17:28.900
You heard her.

00:17:32.950 --> 00:17:35.180
It's cold.

00:17:36.220 --> 00:17:37.890
Oh, she's here!

00:17:37.890 --> 00:17:39.160
Satoru-kun!

00:17:43.060 --> 00:17:45.500
Sorry, Suzukawa-senpai.

00:17:45.500 --> 00:17:47.930
My brother kept saying he wanted to come.

00:17:47.930 --> 00:17:51.290
Maybe you should have just brought him.

00:17:51.290 --> 00:17:54.780
I can't. He's got a cold right now.

00:17:54.780 --> 00:17:56.130
I see.

00:17:56.130 --> 00:17:58.840
It'd be bad if he were out 
in the cold and got worse.

00:17:59.340 --> 00:18:03.350
Also, I wouldn't want you to catch his cold.

00:18:05.090 --> 00:18:06.600
Let's get going, Satoru-kun.

00:18:13.980 --> 00:18:17.000
There's already quite a line.

00:18:17.000 --> 00:18:18.150
Yeah.

00:18:19.610 --> 00:18:20.880
It's pretty.

00:18:20.880 --> 00:18:22.670
Yeah.

00:18:24.300 --> 00:18:25.790
Rino-san?

00:18:26.920 --> 00:18:28.730
This is Satoru-kun.

00:18:28.730 --> 00:18:29.670
My name is Kimijima.

00:18:30.120 --> 00:18:31.410
Hello.

00:18:31.410 --> 00:18:33.880
Did you come here to ring 
the New Year's bell?

00:18:34.200 --> 00:18:35.150
Yeah.

00:18:35.150 --> 00:18:38.550
Is this your first time ringing the bell?

00:18:38.550 --> 00:18:39.820
Yes.

00:18:39.820 --> 00:18:41.520
I'm excited!

00:18:41.520 --> 00:18:43.680
I'm going to get rid of my worldly desires!

00:18:50.950 --> 00:18:53.910
I can hear the temple's bell.

00:18:53.910 --> 00:18:55.070
We should get going.

00:18:56.420 --> 00:18:57.850
Hold on a second.

00:18:57.850 --> 00:19:00.990
I got in a hurry and made things worse.

00:19:04.480 --> 00:19:05.990
Let me see.

00:19:06.520 --> 00:19:08.110
You're a daughter of the shrine priest.

00:19:08.110 --> 00:19:10.640
You can't be like this forever.

00:19:10.640 --> 00:19:13.650
Thanks for everything, Akio-oneechan.

00:19:13.650 --> 00:19:16.130
Jeez, you're hopeless.

00:19:16.130 --> 00:19:18.130
Take that!

00:19:20.060 --> 00:19:22.530
It's pretty late now.

00:19:22.530 --> 00:19:24.720
I need to hurry and find everyone.

00:19:37.110 --> 00:19:39.110
<b>Candy Apples
300 yen</b>

00:19:41.460 --> 00:19:45.940
Chloe-san, what's the difference 
between a temple and a shrine?

00:19:45.940 --> 00:19:47.990
You ring the bell at the temple,

00:19:47.990 --> 00:19:50.150
and at the shrine, there are lots of stalls.

00:19:50.150 --> 00:19:51.250
Really?

00:19:51.550 --> 00:19:57.520
It has more to do with the difference 
between Buddhism and Shinto,

00:19:57.520 --> 00:19:59.940
but I guess we can discuss that later.

00:20:00.520 --> 00:20:03.760
Oh, the arrows that pierce demons!

00:20:04.070 --> 00:20:05.760
Hey, Chloe-san...

00:20:06.500 --> 00:20:08.180
Thank you very much.

00:20:06.760 --> 00:20:12.630
<b>Fortunes</b>

00:20:09.320 --> 00:20:11.020
How wonderful!

00:20:11.020 --> 00:20:12.990
Oh? Chloe.

00:20:12.990 --> 00:20:16.810
Good evening, Akio-san, Mei-san.

00:20:16.810 --> 00:20:20.460
You came to our shrine for 
your first visit of the year?

00:20:20.460 --> 00:20:21.490
Oui.

00:20:21.490 --> 00:20:23.950
I got rid of my worldly desires just a minute ago.

00:20:25.130 --> 00:20:28.140
Oh, you mean the New Year's bell, right?

00:20:28.140 --> 00:20:31.910
We've still got some time 
before the new year starts.

00:20:31.910 --> 00:20:33.830
How about drawing a fortune?

00:20:32.160 --> 00:20:35.000
<b>Fortunes</b>

00:20:33.830 --> 00:20:35.000
A fortune?

00:20:35.470 --> 00:20:39.750
It's a fortune that tells you if you're 
going to have good or bad luck next year.

00:20:39.750 --> 00:20:41.300
I see.

00:20:41.740 --> 00:20:43.550
I want one.

00:20:43.550 --> 00:20:44.510
Me, too.

00:20:45.900 --> 00:20:50.280
"You'll be rewarded if you 
focus on your studies."

00:20:50.280 --> 00:20:50.850
Good.

00:20:51.950 --> 00:20:54.400
How do you read this?

00:20:54.400 --> 00:20:57.400
"Good people come from afar."

00:20:57.400 --> 00:20:59.870
It might be about love, Yulia-san.

00:20:59.870 --> 00:21:02.360
What? Love?

00:21:02.790 --> 00:21:05.610
"What you're looking for is right beside you."

00:21:06.510 --> 00:21:09.110
What does yours say, Chloe-san?

00:21:09.110 --> 00:21:12.400
"Even if a storm comes, it will end."

00:21:12.400 --> 00:21:16.530
This means everything 
works out in the end, right?

00:21:16.530 --> 00:21:19.260
That's what happened this Christmas.

00:21:19.260 --> 00:21:21.410
Yeah, you're right!

00:21:21.410 --> 00:21:25.630
I'm sure something good will 
happen next year, then!

00:21:25.630 --> 00:21:27.870
It's almost the new year.

00:21:31.010 --> 00:21:33.020
10, 9...

00:21:33.380 --> 00:21:34.520
8!

00:21:34.860 --> 00:21:36.020
7!

00:21:36.350 --> 00:21:37.520
6!

00:21:37.520 --> 00:21:39.020
5!

00:21:39.420 --> 00:21:40.520
4!

00:21:40.940 --> 00:21:41.940
3!

00:21:42.370 --> 00:21:43.530
2!

00:21:43.900 --> 00:21:44.990
1!

00:21:46.870 --> 00:21:50.160
Happy New Year!

00:21:50.550 --> 00:21:53.660
Happy New Year!

00:22:06.500 --> 00:22:07.480
Chloe-san.

00:22:07.480 --> 00:22:08.470
Hm?

00:22:08.470 --> 00:22:13.560
I asked you to tell me what was 
bothering you before, right?

00:22:13.560 --> 00:22:14.660
Yeah.

00:22:14.660 --> 00:22:17.390
I have one more thing I want to ask you.

00:22:17.390 --> 00:22:18.580
Is that okay?

00:22:18.580 --> 00:22:20.440
Hm? Sure.

00:22:21.050 --> 00:22:26.110
I'd like to spend New Year's 
with you next year, too.

00:22:27.880 --> 00:22:30.140
Of course!

00:24:01.670 --> 00:24:04.180
Okay, I'm taking it.
